{parent=b}

The integral <Künneth theorem> gives a natural short exact sequence containing tensor and Tor terms. Here all cohomology groups are free abelian, so the Tor terms vanish and the external cup product is a ring isomorphism. Thus
$$
H^*(\mathbb{CP}^2\times\mathbb{CP}^2;\mathbb Z)
\cong\mathbb Z[x,y]/(x^3,y^3),
\qquad |x|=|y|=2.
$$

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

